    <h1>
        The <span class="docs-accent">Entity Component System</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        Crafty's runtime scene stores objects as IDs, state as unmanaged
        component structs, and behavior as ordered systems.
    </p>

    <h2>WorldObject and Scene</h2>

    <p>
        <code>WorldObject</code> is a wrapper around a <code>uint</code>
        identifier. <code>Scene.CreateObject()</code> returns the next
        identifier.
    </p>

    <p>
        The scene owns component stores, renderables, parent relationships,
        and an ordered <code>List&lt;ISystem&gt;</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Components</h2>

    <p>
        Components implement <code>IComponent</code> and are constrained
        as unmanaged structs by the scene's generic component APIs.
        Game examples include <code>Player</code>, <code>Movement</code>,
        <code>Transform</code>, <code>Camera</code>, <code>Inventory</code>,
        and <code>Hotbar</code>.
    </p>

    <p>
        Components are data; systems contain the logic that reads and
        mutates them.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-code-card">
        <div class="docs-code-title">
            <span>COMPONENT SHAPE</span>
            <span>ILLUSTRATIVE PROJECT PATTERN</span>
        </div>

        <pre><code>public struct ExampleComponent : IComponent
{
