    <h2>Systems and hierarchy</h2>

    <p>
        <code>ISystem.Update(ref Scene scene, double deltaTime)</code>
        is the system contract. <code>IGameplaySystem</code> is a marker
        interface used by <code>GameWorld</code> to skip gameplay systems
        while paused.
    </p>

    <p>
        <code>HierarchySystem</code> is added by the scene constructor
        and is responsible for parent-depth ordering and child world
        transforms. Parent relationships are held separately from
        component stores.
    </p>

    <h2>Renderables</h2>

    <p>
        Renderable meshes are stored separately from components in the
        scene's renderable dictionary. A renderable object is expected
        to have a <code>Transform</code> component because the render
        loop reads its transform before drawing it.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-warning">
        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i>

        <div>
            <strong>Important implementation detail</strong>

            <p>
                The component-store implementation returns refs into
                dictionary storage. Avoid retaining component refs
                across operations that may mutate the same store, and
                follow the existing scene/system access patterns.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

